  "body": "## Result\n\nSharp **COPY69** for PR1224's fixed **A2-weight + E6 root-basis nine-normal decoder on standard P112**, with arbitrary independent complex per-root kernel shifts and ordinary transpose. The all-nine-active rational witness has term costs `(1,8,8,8,8,9,9,9,9)` and differs from the dropped-first-term base only by `t_45=-4`.\n\nThis resolves the named A2+E6 follow-up explicitly left in PR1304 and PR1612. It is not a finite coefficient-box extension, the A8-simplex result, retained-coordinate sparse-lift PR1325, or the partition-gauge PR1962/1988 family.\n\n### Proof and evidence\n\nSix forced terms cost 52. The three variable column supports have full binary label rank, so their cost is `27 - sum(kernel dimensions)`. A complete 512-character compatibility census shows that any kernel of dimension at least three forces both other nonzero kernels onto a unique exceptional one-dimensional pair. With the separately handled zero-kernel cases, the total deficiency is at most ten, hence variable cost at least 17. The all-active witness attains 69.\n\nThe package contains the written proof, exact finite certificate, independent geometry/character-basis implementation, actual support-pair charges, 12,544 all-pairs rational identities per checker, semantic negative controls and full chooser/source/replay metadata.\n\nThe complete optimistic **conditional fixed-noncentre** screen already fails at the elementary COPY65 bound. COPY69 sharpens its root to `[1452819253108,1452819253109]/10^15`, even granting fractional rank-nine centres and zero added interface overhead. The independent integer-power bound gives moment `>=15238506806272258653/15232000000000000000 > 1` at `a=1/625`.\n\n**No new physical supplier, selected frontier or kappa is claimed.** The theorem fixes one normal basis and puncture, all-pairs exactness and separate term charges. Other normals, masks, shared physical copies and changed noncentre work remain outside scope.\n\n## Validation\n\nCPython **3.12.12**, darwin arm64, standard library only:\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -B research/a2-e6-nine-normal-floor/verify.py --write\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/a2-e6-nine-normal-floor\n```\n\nObserved: primary certificate PASS; independent geometry/basis and integer-power replay PASS; **six semantic test groups PASS**; optimized `-O` replay PASS; `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`. Parent independently reviewed the proof and replayed all four registered commands before publication. No selected cold replay, Lean/kernel acceptance, independent human review or hosted-CI success is asserted.\n\n## Provenance and scope\n\nOnly `research/a2-e6-nine-normal-floor/` is added. Base `e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a`; independent seed `814c825e12629ac65e009a4beab63757`, complex-mechanisms / complex-rank-shape-decoder. Explicit changed scope: the named support-family obstruction rather than a physical synthesis success. Full original draw is preserved in SELECTION.json.\n\nCredit joaqcoo / PR1224 for the family and normal form; Philipp/mightyOil / PR1248, commdata2338 / PR1304, and Hanson Sun/bbMisk / PR1612 for the deficiency approach and handoff; DreamingOfClouds / PR717/595/446 for the decoder/COPY model; Joel Pulikkan/GamingPuzzled / PR620 for coordinate COPY64; themilkman216 / PR968 and woklerx / PR1077 for surrounding bounds; Sagar Thakrar / PR1012 and Douglas Colkitt / PR1240 for coverage and ceiling accounting. Frozen inputs remain unchanged and hash-pinned.\n\n[Coordination claim](#research-claim-and-completion-record). Final cached overlap and targeted live merged-head/search checks are recorded in TASK.json, including coverage limits.\n\nPrepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, proof, implementation, checking and writing. Apache-2.0.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE \u2014 seed 814c825e12629ac65e009a4beab63757. PR #2061 https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2061 at eed23989eddf7ec0b2c24d9e3794d0fca53f11ab proves sharp separate COPY69 for PR1224 fixed A2-weight + E6 root-basis nine-normal decoder on standard P112, allowing arbitrary independent complex row shifts. All nine terms active: (1,8,8,8,8,9,9,9,9), t45=-4 only. Complete binary compatibility gives deficiency sum <=10 and variable cost17 plus forced52. Conditional fixed-noncentre optimistic budget fails even with all centre mass at rank9 and zero additional overhead; no new supplier or kappa. CPython3.12 registered replay passed primary/independent checks,12544 identities per checker,6 test groups and optimized replay; parent independently reviewed/replayed before publication. Base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a. Credit joaqcoo PR1224, mightyOil PR1248, commdata2338 PR1304, bbMisk PR1612, decoder and coverage/ceiling lineage in package. No hosted-CI success, proof-assistant or independent human review claimed.\n",
